    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d189">

                <pb facs="0160" n="140" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg140"/>

                <head>Mr. Dayton to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 526.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-08-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 23, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The enclosed slip is cut from Galignani of
                    this morning, and I receive at the same time like information as to the
                    projected trial trips of these vessels from our consul at Nantes. There is a
                    thin iron plating, it is said, on the inside of these vessels not more than an
                    inch at most in thickness. I have given this information to Captain Rodgers, of
                    the Iroquois, who is now at Havre repairing the boilers of his ship, and advised
                    him to appear off the port of Nantes and consult with our consul at that
                    port.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WM. L. DAYTON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, &amp;c., &amp;c.,
                        &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d189-a1.xml" xpointer="d189-a1"/>
